WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.375
A broken kiln cancels Saturday's workshop.

00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:05.301
Mina bought two seats.

00:00:05.321 --> 00:00:09.609
Her sister can join Sunday; Mina needs her ticket refunded.

00:00:09.629 --> 00:00:13.478
Raincheck gives the studio one place to carry both choices through.

00:00:14.478 --> 00:00:16.712
Start with the original payment.

00:00:16.732 --> 00:00:23.655
Raincheck creates a one-hundred-and-thirty-six-dollar PayPal sandbox order for two sixty-eight-dollar tickets.

00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:26.896
A separate virtual buyer approves it in PayPal.

00:00:26.916 --> 00:00:31.206
The approval happens in another tab; account details stay private.

00:00:32.206 --> 00:00:34.244
Capture the approved order.

00:00:34.264 --> 00:00:43.388
Raincheck reads the order and the capture, checks the booking reference, currency and exact amount, then attaches that verified payment to Mina's booking.

00:00:43.408 --> 00:00:46.318
Every refund starts with this original payment.

00:00:47.326 --> 00:00:49.601
Here is a newly worded reply.

00:00:49.621 --> 00:00:55.108
A live open-weight model on Nebius extracts one Sunday seat and one ticket refund.

00:00:55.128 --> 00:01:01.048
Raincheck checks the last available place and computes sixty-eight dollars from the saved ticket price.

00:01:01.068 --> 00:01:03.070
The teacher reviews the proposal.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.540
Run the plan.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:14.210
Raincheck saves one request identifier, holds Sunday's seat, and asks PayPal to refund sixty-eight dollars against the original capture.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.398
PayPal returns completed.

00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:21.710
The new seat is confirmed and the outcome includes the refund receipt and a message ready to send.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.550
Reload the workspace.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.434
The captured payment, the refund and the seat stay together.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:32.960
An independent refund lookup matches the stored operation and amount.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:36.722
For a whole cancelled class, start with the batch.

00:01:36.742 --> 00:01:42.694
This five-household rehearsal uses simulated payments inside the real AG Studio workspace.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.023
Ask the Studio analyst to find the seat conflict.

00:01:47.043 --> 00:01:52.705
It reads the saved plans and filters Sunday: Mina and Elliot want the same final place.

00:01:52.725 --> 00:01:55.662
The custom capacity widget shows the shortfall.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.971
Open Mina's agreed plan in the confirmation desk.

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:06.654
Interrupt the refund response, then return to the batch: one seat is held and sixty-eight dollars is in progress.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.532
Resume the saved operation and refresh.

00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:14.163
Mina is settled; Elliot still needs a new choice.

00:02:14.183 --> 00:02:17.592
The seat and money columns read the same saved outcome.

00:02:17.612 --> 00:02:21.398
Try Raincheck, or run both modules from the setup guides.
